1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:05,920
his eyes very wide open for we have reason to think that some of Snowball's

2
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:11,640
secret agents are lurking among us at this moment.

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:16,840
>> Four days later in the late afternoon, Napoleon ordered all the animals to

4
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,319
assemble in the yard.

5
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:23,239
When they were all gathered together, Napoleon emerged from the farmhouse

6
00:00:23,239 --> 00:00:28,239
wearing both his medals, for he had recently awarded himself Animal Hero,

7
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:33,520
First Class, and Animal Hero, Second Class.

8
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:38,640
With his nine huge dogs frisking round him and uttering growls that sent

9
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,039
shivers down all the animals' spines.

10
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:47,199
They all cowered silently in their places, seeming to know in advance that some

11
00:00:47,199 --> 00:00:50,239
terrible thing was about to happen.

12
00:00:50,239 --> 00:00:54,119
Napoleon stood sternly surveying his audience.

13
00:00:54,119 --> 00:00:57,800
Then he uttered a high-pitched whimper.

14
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:02,760
Immediately the dogs bounded forward, seized four of the pigs by the ear, and

15
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:08,239
dragged them, squealing with pain and terror, to Napoleon's feet.

16
00:01:08,239 --> 00:01:14,159
The pigs' ears were bleeding. The dogs had tasted blood, and for a few moments,

17
00:01:14,159 --> 00:01:17,359
they appeared to go quite mad.

18
00:01:17,359 --> 00:01:23,640
To the amazement of everybody, three of them flung themselves upon Boxer.

19
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:29,560
Boxer saw them coming and put out his great hoof, caught a dog in midair, and

20
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,880
pinned him to the ground.

21
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:38,960
The dog shrieked for mercy, and the other two fled with their tails between their legs.

22
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:45,840
Boxer looked at Napoleon to know whether he should crush the dog to death or let it go.

23
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:52,920
Napoleon appeared to change countenance, and sharply ordered Boxer to let the dog go.

24
00:01:52,920 --> 00:02:00,319
Whereat Boxer lifted his hoof, and the dog slunk away, bruised and howling.

25
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:03,239
Presently the tumult died down.

26
00:02:03,239 --> 00:02:10,319
The four pigs waited, trembling with guilt written on every line of their countenances.

27
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:14,239
Napoleon now called upon them to confess their crimes.

28
00:02:14,239 --> 00:02:20,479
They were the same four pigs as had protested when Napoleon abolished the Sunday meetings.

29
00:02:20,479 --> 00:02:24,279
Without any further prompting, they confessed that they had been secretly in

30
00:02:24,279 --> 00:02:29,239
touch with Snowball ever since his expulsion, that they had collaborated with him in

31
00:02:29,239 --> 00:02:33,720
destroying the windmill, and that they had entered into an agreement with him

32
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,000
to hand over Animal Farm to Mr.

33
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,479
Frederick.

34
00:02:37,479 --> 00:02:41,319
They added that Snowball had privately admitted to them that he had been

35
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:45,119
Jones's secret agent for years past.

36
00:02:45,119 --> 00:02:48,760
When they had finished their confession, the dogs promptly tore their throats

37
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:53,840
out, and in a terrible voice, Napoleon demanded whether any other animal had

38
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:56,119
anything to confess.

39
00:02:56,119 --> 00:02:59,640
The three hens who had been the ringleaders in the attempted rebellion

40
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:04,159
over the eggs now came forward and stated that Snowball had appeared to

41
00:03:04,159 --> 00:03:09,720
them in a dream and incited them to disobey Napoleon's orders.

42
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:12,479
They too were slaughtered.

43
00:03:12,479 --> 00:03:17,720
Then a goose came forward and confessed to having secreted six ears of corn

44
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:22,279
during the last year's harvest and eaten them in the night.

45
00:03:22,279 --> 00:03:26,720
Then a sheep confessed to having urinated in the drinking pool,

46
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:30,640
urged to do this, so she said, by Snowball.

47
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:35,600
And two other sheep confessed to having murdered an old ram, an especially

48
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:40,600
devoted follower of Napoleon, by chasing him round and round a bonfire when he

49
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,960
was suffering from a cough.

50
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:46,039
They were all slain on the spot.

51
00:03:46,039 --> 00:03:50,880
And so the tale of confessions and executions went on until there was a

52
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:55,600
pile of corpses lying before Napoleon's feet, and the air was heavy with the

53
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:01,399
smell of blood, which had been unknown there since the expulsion of Jones.

54
00:04:01,399 --> 00:04:05,760
When it was all over, the remaining animals, except for the pigs and dogs,

55
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,720
crept away in a body.

56
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,239
They were shaken and miserable.

57
00:04:10,239 --> 00:04:14,239
They did not know which was more shocking, the treachery of the animals

58
00:04:14,239 --> 00:04:20,439
who had leagued themselves with Snowball, or the cruel retribution they had just witnessed.

59
00:04:20,439 --> 00:04:24,840
In the old days, there had often been scenes of bloodshed equally terrible,

60
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:28,920
but it seemed to all of them that it was far worse now that it was happening

61
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:30,920
among themselves.

62
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,000
Since Jones had left the farm until
